          "answer": 0,
          "why": "Conflicts mean over-constraining: two rules demand different values for one attribute. The fix is editorial, not additive \u2014 remove or demote, never pile on. Compression resistance and content hugging priorities resolve 'label vs fixed width' fights declaratively. Interviewers want the systematic read-the-log habit, not guessing.",
          "hint": "The log names the fighters. What does it mean when two constraints claim the same attribute, and which one represents your real intent?",
