          "answer": 0,
          "why": "UIViewRepresentable is the sanctioned bridge: create once, update declaratively. The Coordinator is the key insight \u2014 UIKit's delegate/target-action world needs an object to receive callbacks, and the coordinator (owned by SwiftUI) translates them into state changes. updateUIView must be idempotent since SwiftUI calls it on every state change.",
          "hint": "UIKit speaks delegate; SwiftUI speaks state. What object stands between them translating both directions?",
