            "Cache images in a global dictionary \u2014 once loaded, flashing stops.",
            "Disable cell reuse so each row keeps its own image view forever.",
            "Load images synchronously in `cellForRowAt` \u2014 ordering is then guaranteed."
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "why": "The bug is a race between reuse and completion: row 5's image arrives after the cell now shows row 42. Cancellation (Task.cancel, Operation.cancel, or invalidating a load token in prepareForReuse) plus a 'still the right item?' check before assignment is the full answer. This is also where SwiftUI's `.task` modifier shines \u2014 it auto-cancels when the view disappears.",
          "hint": "Whose image is the cell showing when the slow request finally completes \u2014 and how does the cell know it is stale?",
          "objectives": [
            "Design cancellation into async UI work"
